# Project Documentation Maintenance

Read `AGENTS.md` at the start of every session on this repo.

## Documentation files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `AGENTS.md` | Agent onboarding, stack, scope, workflow |
| `DESIGN.md` | UI/UX and product design decisions (append-only log) |
| `LEARNINGS.md` | Session learnings (newest first) |
| `docs/specs/v1-technical-specification.md` | Canonical V1 spec |
| `docs/README.md` | Documentation index |

## When to update

- **Scope/architecture/API change** → update spec + `DESIGN.md` decision log
- **UI/UX decision** → append to `DESIGN.md`
- **Session end or significant discovery** → prepend entry to `LEARNINGS.md`
- **New doc file** → add to `docs/README.md`, `AGENTS.md` map, and `docs/CHANGELOG.md`
- **Onboarding/stack change** → update `AGENTS.md` and `README.md`
- **New risk or open decision** → add row to `docs/risk-register.md`
- **Any markdown prose edit** → run `@humanize-docs` before finishing

## Dual sync (local + Notion)

Local filesystem is source of truth. After meaningful doc changes:
1. Commit to git (when user requests)
2. Sync summary to Notion Project Hub

Use skill `@maintain-project-docs` for the full workflow.

## V1 scope guard

Do not expand V1 scope (groups, auto-tracking, algorithms) without explicit user approval. Document deferred items in spec §2 only.

## Spec-first development

No feature implementation until V1 spec is approved. Reference spec section numbers in PR descriptions.
